C:/Users/mpeet/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/363c499c6332a503/874c85cb-c18d-4876-bea3-39cdd053e21f/scratchpad/sop/tex/sopvar_duality_pruning_notes.tex:495:
  - Every executive of \code{executives\_sopvar} runs the same steps, the LPI being the only variable part: convert the PIE operators to containers; declare the storage as the stock executive does (\code{exec\_tools\_sop}); form the blocks of the LPI; declare the slack with \code{lpi\_ineq\_sop} and \code{like} the storage, or the stock slack when \code{settings.sop.slack = 'stock'}; solve inside the degree loop; read the solution, the dual kernel (Sec.~\ref{sec:sdpdual}) and the SDP shape; and in one variable evaluate the numerical counterpart. The stock outputs come first, in the stock order, and \code{info} last.
  + Every executive of \code{executives} runs the same steps, the LPI being the only variable part: convert the PIE operators to containers; declare the storage as the stock executive does (\code{exec\_tools}); form the blocks of the LPI; declare the slack with \code{lpi\_ineq} and \code{like} the storage, or the stock slack when \code{settings.sop.slack = 'stock'}; solve inside the degree loop; read the solution, the dual kernel (Sec.~\ref{sec:sdpdual}) and the SDP shape; and in one variable evaluate the numerical counterpart. The stock outputs come first, in the stock order, and \code{info} last.
C:/Users/mpeet/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/363c499c6332a503/874c85cb-c18d-4876-bea3-39cdd053e21f/scratchpad/sop/tex/sopvar_duality_pruning_notes.tex:499:
  - A certificate is an upper bound; the executives set a lower bound beside it. \code{pie\_disc\_sop} forms the Galerkin matrix of each 4-PI operator in the orthonormal basis $\R^{m_0}\oplus\mrm{span}\{p_j(s)e_k\}$, $p_j$ the shifted Legendre polynomials of degree $\le N$ on $I$, with exact pairings: the kernels are polynomial, so Gauss--Legendre quadrature with $N+d_{\max}+3$ nodes on the recurrence-evaluated basis integrates every entry exactly. Orthonormality makes the matrix of a composition the product of the matrices up to the truncation and the $L_2$ norms the Euclidean norms of coefficient vectors, so no mass matrix enters. \code{pie\_witness\_sop} evaluates the frequency response $G(i\omega)=C(i\omega T-A)^{-1}B+D$ on a logarithmic grid refined around its maximum (a lower bound on the gain, with the worst input), the generalized eigenvalues of $(A,T)$ (the decay rate) and the Lyapunov $H_2$ norm. The first version expanded the Legendre basis in monomials and summed closed-form moments; its coefficients grow as $4^N$, every digit was lost beyond $N=12$, and the default $N=24$ produced spurious eigenvalues ($+548$ for a plant at $-4.93$) before the quadrature version replaced it. Never evaluate an orthogonal polynomial through its monomial coefficients.
  + A certificate is an upper bound; the executives set a lower bound beside it. \code{pie\_disc} forms the Galerkin matrix of each 4-PI operator in the orthonormal basis $\R^{m_0}\oplus\mrm{span}\{p_j(s)e_k\}$, $p_j$ the shifted Legendre polynomials of degree $\le N$ on $I$, with exact pairings: the kernels are polynomial, so Gauss--Legendre quadrature with $N+d_{\max}+3$ nodes on the recurrence-evaluated basis integrates every entry exactly. Orthonormality makes the matrix of a composition the product of the matrices up to the truncation and the $L_2$ norms the Euclidean norms of coefficient vectors, so no mass matrix enters. \code{pie\_witness} evaluates the frequency response $G(i\omega)=C(i\omega T-A)^{-1}B+D$ on a logarithmic grid refined around its maximum (a lower bound on the gain, with the worst input), the generalized eigenvalues of $(A,T)$ (the decay rate) and the Lyapunov $H_2$ norm. The first version expanded the Legendre basis in monomials and summed closed-form moments; its coefficients grow as $4^N$, every digit was lost beyond $N=12$, and the default $N=24$ produced spurious eigenvalues ($+548$ for a plant at $-4.93$) before the quadrature version replaced it. Never evaluate an orthogonal polynomial through its monomial coefficients.
